From c8f236cca671fed817ea77f5095c4521cc6eb223 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:16:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Material properties of the generic-parallel interface

- A material property generated by the generic-parallel interface is
  recognized when it is loaded: interface, version of the functions,
  backend and memory space are read, and the function of a set of points
  is loaded (`batch_fct`) instead of the function of a point, which is
  refused for such a library, and conversely.
- `evaluate(values, mp, inputs[, location, policy])` evaluates a material
  property on a set of points, the inputs being uniform or given point by
  point: by one call for a material property generated by the
  generic-parallel interface, point by point on the host otherwise, as
  `integrate` for behaviours. The location of the values is checked
  against the memory space of the material property, invalid arguments
  raise exceptions, and the statuses keep the meaning of the generic
  interface.
- `MemoryLocation` moves to the `mgis` namespace (`MGIS/MemoryLocation.hxx`),
  with the accessibility rule written once for behaviours and material
  properties.
- The CMake functions building the libraries of the generic-parallel
  interface (behaviours, models and material properties) share their
  implementation (`cmake/modules/generic-parallel.cmake`).
---
